@startuml
' ============================================================
' Sequence Diagram - Log Event Pipeline
' Any Service → RabbitMQ → Logger Consumer → OpenSearch
' (no PostgreSQL — OpenSearch is primary store)
' ============================================================

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #333333
  ActorBorderColor #333333
  LifeLineBorderColor #333333
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
  ParticipantBorderColor #333333
}

title Sequence Diagram: Log Event Pipeline (Event-Driven)

actor "Any Service\n(AUTH, SMS, etc.)" as Service
queue "RabbitMQ\n(queue: log.events)" as MQ
participant "Logger\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "OpenSearch\n(index: log-events)" as OS

== Step 1: Publish Log Event ==

Service -> MQ : PUBLISH log.events\n{ eventId, source, level, action,\n  message, timestamp }
activate MQ

note right of Service
  Service generates UUID
  Non-blocking publish
  Returns eventId immediately
end note

Service --> Service : Return eventId

== Step 2: Consumer Receives Message ==

MQ -> Consumer : CONSUME log.events
activate Consumer

Consumer -> Consumer : Parse JSON message\ninto LogEvent

== Step 3: Index to OpenSearch ==

Consumer -> OS : INDEX log-events\n{ eventId, source, level, action,\n  message, input, output,\n  error, exception, traceId,\n  userId, timestamp }
activate OS
OS --> Consumer : Indexed
deactivate OS

== Step 4: Acknowledge Message ==

Consumer -> MQ : ACK
deactivate Consumer
deactivate MQ

== Error Handling ==

note over Consumer
  If OpenSearch indexing fails:
  - Retry with exponential backoff (3 attempts)
  - Log error and ACK to prevent poison pill
end note

@enduml
